        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare visceral arteriovenous malformation characterized by dilated and tortuous feeding arteries and veins of the gallblader. Patients present with abdominal pain. Association with hepatocellular carcinoma in some patients have been reported."
